      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 46-year-old-man received high dose chemotherapy and an autologous stem-cell transplant for multiple plasmacytoma. He had a prolonged period of pancytopenia post-transplantation, which was thought to be due to a suboptimal dose of transplanted stem cells in combination with the effects of interferon therapy and an altered bone marrow microenvironment. Twenty-eight months after the transplant he was found to be hyperthyroid. Anti-thyroid therapy has led to a sustained improvement in his pancytopenia."},
